-+## Changed
-+
-+- Copied `pauses.json`, `recertifications.json`, `notices.json`,
-+  `focused_runs.json`, `mutation_picks.json`, `mutation_survivors.json`,
-+  `validator_runs.json`, `validator_findings.json` and `link_findings.json`
-+  from the change's `golden/` folder into `crates/kernel/storage/tests/golden/`
-+  byte-for-byte.
-+- Added `crates/kernel/storage/tests/history_corpus.rs` (189 lines). It builds
-+  the read model once with `build_read_model` under
-+  `env!("CARGO_TARGET_TMPDIR")`, reads each of the nine event tables in table
-+  order, keeps the rows whose folder is numbered 014 to 209, and compares them
-+  row by row with the golden file, naming the table, the row's `change`, the
-+  column and both values on a mismatch. Row counts are checked per table. The
-+  test carries `#[ignore = "corpus test: reads the live archive"]` and its doc
-+  names `Covers: rust-storage/golden-event-table-rows`.
-+
-+## Deviated
-+
-+- No source correction was needed: every golden row already agreed with
-+  `src/read/` and `src/model/`, so no line in `src/` changed and no
-+  `tests/history_cases.rs` was added. The existing fast counterpart for the
-+  same requirement remains `tests/read_model_history.rs` plus the history
-+  fixture, as the delta spec's "History fixture rows" says.
-+- The test parses the golden JSON with `serde_json` and compares numbers as
-+  `f64`; every value matched, so the fallback of reading a number from the
-+  event line's text was not needed.
-+
-+## Next
-+
-+None.
-+
